gradient(135deg,#0a0f1e,#1a1040);padding:25px;border-radius:15px;border:1px solid #00c9a7;color:#e2e8f0;\">\n\n### What we did:\n1. **Optuna HPO** — 50 trials per model (LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost) tuned with MAE objective using TPE sampler.\n2. **Rich Spatio-Temporal Features** — Cross-camera aggregations (mean, std, min, max, sum), lag/lead features, rolling statistics, EMA, velocity features, cyclical time encodings, and prayer-time proximity indicators.\n3. **MAE-Optimized Training** — All models use `objective='mae'` / `loss_function='MAE'` matching the competition metric.\n4. **Per-Gap-Type Specialization** — Separate models for forecast/hidden/hidden-future/missing gaps, blended with global model.\n5. **Meta-Stacking Ensemble** — Ridge regression on OOF predictions + interactions, compared with inverse-MAE weighted average.\n6. **Recording-Aware CV** — GroupKFold to avoid leaking temporal patterns across folds.\n\n### Generalization strategy:\n- 🩺 **Generalization Scorecard** — Multi-signal overfit/underfit detector\n- KS-test comparing OOF vs Test distributions\n- Per-gap-type MAE breakdown to find weak spots\n- Residual analysis for bias detection\n- Early stopping (200 rounds) with native NaN handling\n- Non-negative clipping (crowd counts ≥ 0)\n\n</div>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null}]}